Original commit body from 0ecb2c0fc28840cce534f74f12efb95da160d0ef:

WI-nukut. measure-call-escape-cause.py filtered escape sites down to call
nodes with a bare string comparison against the PYTHON node type:

    if cache[sym].get(line) != "call":
        continue

Go's call nodes are call_expression / deferred_call / go_statement, so for a
Go repository the filter discarded every site. caddy printed

    === CALL-node escape sites: 0 ===

while the instrument's own positive control in the same run reported 78,600
edges offered and 236 escape events captured. A zero under a live control is
the shape a reader trusts; read literally it says Go produces no call-node
escape sites, which is a claim about a LANGUAGE from an instrument that never
looked at that language.

MIXED-LANGUAGE REPOS ARE WHERE IT WAS LEAST VISIBLE, and that is why the first
blast-radius estimate was wrong. kserve is 34 python sites and 14 go; pretix is
15 python and 5 javascript. The dropped sites hide behind the python ones that
still come through, so the arm looks like it worked.

THE FIX IS NOT "ADD GO'S SPELLING" — that repeats the mistake one language
later. _CALL_NODE_TYPES is a declared per-language map whose every entry is
grounded in CFG output actually observed across pretix / kserve / caddy /
alertmanager, and a language with NO entry now REFUSES THE TABLE (exit 2),
naming the language and how many sites went unclassified. That is the contract
measure-escape-closing-ceiling.py already holds for its own monkeypatch: a
number from an instrument that could not see part of its population is worse
than no number, because it reads as a finding. javascript is deliberately
absent rather than guessed — the corpus produced no call-shaped node for it.

BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, live repro on the merged tree:

    caddy, before: === CALL-node escape sites: 0 ===
    caddy, after : === CALL-node escape sites: 8 ===
                     1-NO EDGE EMITTED (INV-mumov)          4  50.0%
                     4a-KEY PRESENT, NO SUMMARY             3  37.5%
                     3a-NO RECEIVER TYPE (INV-linub)        1  12.5%

The Go cause distribution inverts Python's, where INV-linub carries 76.5% on
pretix — a per-language difference the blindness was hiding entirely.

